# Line endings are pinned HERE, not left to each machine's core.autocrlf.
# A Windows host checks text out as CRLF; Cowork's git runs in a Linux VM over
# the SAME folder with no autocrlf, rehashes every file, and reports each CRLF
# one as modified — a dirty tree nobody made, which rotate's gate then refuses.
# LF everywhere means both gits read identical bytes. Stays at root after
# genesis, like .gitignore: it governs the adopter's own repo from then on.
* text=auto eol=lf
